    "created_at": "2017-03-14T17:23:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-14T19:37:55Z",
    "body": "Just to be clear. Edge and Firefox have long behavior-ish (edge is `round()`, firefox is `ToInt32()`/`clamp`-ish), but they would still need to slightly adapt. Forcing to int/long, would slightly change the behavior on the \"round to 1\" issue for every implementation. Which I think is the correct thing, but just to be clear that there will be a very small change everywhere (namely, removing the \"`if (w < 1) w = 1`\" code).\r\n\r\nFor example: `getImageData(0, 0, 0.1, 1.5)`. Right now, the considered sizes on each browser would be: Edge: `(1,2)`, Firefox: `(1,1)`, Chrome/Safari/Opera: `(1, 1.5)`. Defining getImageData as long, which is good, would mean to consider this `(0,1)` and throw an exception.\r\n\r\nThat said, I'd be ok with filing a heads up bug on Webkit, Blink and Gecko.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
